<h3 class="faq-item__q">What lighting is recommended for cold storage and grocery?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Cold storage facilities require vapor-tight, IP-rated LED fixtures that perform reliably in sub-zero temperatures without warm-up times. Grocery aisles benefit from high-CRI linear lighting to enhance product appearance.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">Are there DLC rebates for cold storage retrofits?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Yes, upgrading legacy cold storage lighting to DLC-listed LEDs yields excellent utility rebates. LEDs emit less heat than traditional sources, generating secondary savings by reducing the load on refrigeration systems.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">What controls do cold storage facilities need?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Cold storage areas require low-temperature-rated occupancy sensors to ensure lights are only active when forklifts or personnel are present, preventing unnecessary heat generation.</p>
</article>
